Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: stop emitting wpa_supplicant globals only qcn-app-extns understands

The QCA wifi-scripts (qca/feeds/wlan-open/mac80211/wifi-scripts) write
the wpa_supplicant configuration for every supplicant-managed vif (sta,
adhoc, and 802.11s mesh) with five QCA-specific global fields appended
unconditionally after the network block:

    CSwOpts=$CSwOpts
    athnewind=$athnewind
    rptr_mgr_mode=$rptr_mgr_mode
    channel=$channel
    uplink_csa=$uplink_csa

These are parsed only by the QCA wifi extensions in wpa_supplicant
(qcn-app-extns).  This build ships the wpad-mesh-*-noextns variant on
purpose (qcn-app-extns is not part of the imported QCA source drop, see
custom-packages.conf), so its config reader rejects any unknown global
field and drops the entire file:

    Successfully initialized wpa_supplicant
    Failed to read or parse configuration '/var/run/wpa_supplicant-mesh6g.conf'

wpa_supplicant then exits and netifd leaves the vdev DOWN: an 802.11s
interface (mode mesh, which the scripts route through
mac80211_setup_supplicant because wpa_supplicant -vmesh succeeds) never
joins its mesh and carries no traffic.

Not emitting the five fields equals the extension defaults
(athnewind=0, rptr_mgr_mode=1, no CS options, no uplink CSA, channel
unset), i.e. exactly the values the on-device configuration contained,
so behaviour without the extensions is unchanged.  ppe_vp and
wps_cred_add_sae are kept: both are understood by this wpa_supplicant.

---
--- a/qca/feeds/wlan-open/mac80211/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/hostapd.sh
+++ b/qca/feeds/wlan-open/mac80211/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/hostapd.sh
@@ -2373,11 +2373,17 @@
 	if [ "$key_mgmt" = "WPS" ]; then
 		echo "wps_cred_processing=1" >> "$_config"
 	else
+		# CSwOpts, athnewind, rptr_mgr_mode, channel and uplink_csa are parsed
+		# only by the QCA wifi extensions in wpa_supplicant (qcn-app-extns).
+		# This build ships the -noextns variant, whose config reader rejects
+		# the whole file on an unknown global field ("Failed to read or parse
+		# configuration"), so an 802.11s mesh interface never comes up.  Not
+		# emitting them equals the extension defaults (athnewind=0,
+		# rptr_mgr_mode=1, no CS options, no uplink CSA).
 		cat >> "$_config" <<EOF
 $mesh_ctrl_interface
 $user_mpm
 $disable_csa_dfs
-CSwOpts=$CSwOpts
 $saepwe
 $dpp1905connector
 $rsn_override
@@ -2400,10 +2406,6 @@
 	$smd_id
 	$smd_ptk_mode
 }
-athnewind=$athnewind
-rptr_mgr_mode=$rptr_mgr_mode
-channel=$channel
-uplink_csa=$uplink_csa
 EOF
 	fi
 	return 0
